24785:
For an ideal solution the vapour mole fraction follows y_A = \frac{x_A P_A^\circ}{x_A P_A^\circ + (1 - x_A) P_B^\circ}
Substitution gives 0.8 = \frac{55 x_A}{55 x_A + 15 \times (1 - x_A)} = \frac{55 x_A}{40 x_A + 15}
Rearranging gives 32 x_A + 12 = 55 x_A so 23 x_A = 12 and x_A = \frac{12}{23} = 0.5217
This value matches option C → (C)

